			},
			"source": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "A public or "
						},
						{
							"type": "emphasis",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "symmetric key"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " that is trusted because it is built directly into hardware or software or securely provisioned via out-of-band means rather than because it is vouched for by another trusted entity (e.g., in a "
						},
						{
							"type": "emphasis",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "public-key"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " certificate). A trust anchor may have name or policy constraints that limit its scope."
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"translation": {
				"content": [
					{
						"type": "paragraph",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "ほかの信頼された実体による保証 (例: "
							},
							{
								"type": "emphasis",
								"children": [
									{
										"type": "text",
										"value": "公開鍵"
									}
								]
							},
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "証明書) によってではなく、ハードウェアやソフトウェアに直接組み込まれているか、帯域外の手段で安全にプロビジョニングされていることによって信頼される、公開鍵または"
							},
							{
								"type": "emphasis",
								"children": [
									{
										"type": "text",
										"value": "対称鍵"
									}
								]
							},
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "。トラストアンカーには、その範囲を制限する名前やポリシーの制約が付いていることがある。"
							}
						]
					}
				],
				"sourceHash": "e8fc5b07aefef1f5f6ed068a49df11b866576568f659caff7fe06ef23af610a4"
			}
		}
	],
